Fix implemented. Unit tests of the diff and cursor positioning show correct behavior.
However, the bug still manifests in ttyd/xterm.js during navigation - may be a separate issue.

## Overview
Set up filesystem watching with proper debouncing and filtering.

## Implementation (src/watch/watcher.ts)

```typescript
class FileSystemWatcher {
  private watcher: FSWatcher
  private pendingPaths: Set<string> = new Set()

  start(vaultPath: string) {
    this.watcher = new FSWatcher({
      persistent: true,
      ignoreInitial: true,
      ignored: ['**/node_modules/**', '**/.git/**', '**/.kimmi/**'],
      awaitWriteFinish: { stabilityThreshold: 500 }
    })

    this.watcher.on('all', (event, path) => {
      this.pendingPaths.add(path)
      this.scheduleSync()  // 5s debounce
    })
  }
}
```

## Acceptance Criteria
- Reliable detection of file changes
- No infinite loops
- Proper resource cleanup

## Overview
Queue and apply database changes back to the filesystem with debouncing.

## Implementation (src/watch/write-queue.ts)

```typescript
class WriteQueue {
  private pending: Map<string, PendingWrite> = new Map()

  queue(write: PendingWrite) {
    this.pending.set(write.path, write)  // coalesce
    this.scheduleFlush()  // 3s debounce
  }

  private async flush() {
    // Mark in-flight to prevent watch re-trigger
    for (const write of writes) {
      inFlightWrites.add(write.path)
      await fs.writeFile(write.path, write.content)
    }
  }
}
```

## Acceptance Criteria
- Database changes reflected in files
- No infinite loops
- Minimal file writes (coalescing)

